at-indexed δ-cover V_i of F. Put ρ_i=ediam(V_i), finite since ρ_i≤δ. Let A_i=π₁(V_i) and B_i=π₂(V_i). For each t∈[0,1], set W^t_i=A_i if t∈J_i, and ∅ otherwise, where J_i is an open interval enclosing B_i with length at most ρ_i+η_i. If B_i≠∅, boundedness and diam(B_i)≤ρ_i give finite infimum and supremum; enlarging the closed interval between them by total width η_i yields such J_i. If B_i=∅, choose an interval of length η_i. Since V covers F, for every x∈E and t∈[0,1] some i has (x,t)∈V_i; then x∈A_i and t∈B_i⊆J_i, so W^t covers E, and ediam(W^t_i)≤ρ_i. Thus by the definition of infimum, pointwise in t, c_s=C_s(E,δ)≤∑'ᵢ 1_{J_i∩[0,1]}(t)ρ_i^s. This is the cover/slice comparison for this arbitrary cover, not an assertion about a selected cover. For ε>0 put η_i=ε2^(−i−1)/(1+ρ_i^s). Extend the inequality to ℝ by multiplying its left side by 1_[0,1](t); both sides vanish outside [0,1]. Let ν=volume.restrict([0,1]); M011 gives ν(ℝ)=1. For every i the set J_i∩[0,1] is Borel because J_i is open and [0,1] is closed, hence its indicator is measurable by the definition of the Borel measurable space (preimages of {1} and {0} are respectively this set and its complement, both Borel). Multiplication by the constant ρ_i^s preserves measurability: the resulting function has just the two values ρ_i^s and 0, with Borel level preimages (or is constant if the coefficient is zero). A measurable ENNReal-valued function is AEMeasurable by taking itself as the almost-everywhere measurable representative. This proves separately for every i the AEMeasurability required by M002; it is not inferred merely from the Borel-set phrase. Integrate the nonnegative pointwise inequality. M009 gives monotonicity, M002 applies to the countable Nat-indexed family just verified, and M010 evaluates the constant left integral and the individual constant multiples, yielding c_s≤∑'ᵢρ_i^s ν(J_i∩[0,1]). By restriction, ν(J_i∩[0,1])=volume(J_i∩[0,1]). This set is contained in a closed interval of length ≤ρ_i+η_i (use the enclosing interval for nonempty B_i, and a singleton bound when the intersection is empty); M013 monotonicity and M011's interval-volume formula imply ν(J_i∩[0,1])≤ofReal(ρ_i+η_i). Therefore c_s≤∑'ᵢρ_i^(s+1)+∑'ᵢη_iρ_i^s≤∑'ᵢρ_i^(s+1)+ε, since η_iρ_i^s≤ε2^(−i−1) and these weights sum to 1. Let ε tend to zero (if the cover's cost is infinite the comparison is immediate) to obtain C_s(E,δ)≤∑'ᵢρ_i^(s+1) for this arbitrary cover V. Taking the infimum over exactly all Nat-indexed δ-covers V of F gives C_s(E,δ)≤C_(s+1)(F,δ). As δ tends to zero the left side diverges, so the right scale contents diverge, and M008 gives H^(s+1)(F)=∞. M014 implies s+1≤dim_H(F); taking the supremum over 0<s<D gives D+1≤dim_H(F).\"}]}}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read an explicitly frozen task document by ID; no other local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Report exact status, location, explanation, basis, partial_progress. SUBSTANTIVE_GAP or SUSPECTED_GAP stops for an actual unsupported mathematical implication; give its premises, conclusion and mathematical grounds. SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE or INPUT_CONFLICT stops for a real source-access/original-input obstacle. Ordinary unfinished drafting, source registration or format work must use TASK_INCOMPLETE: this records progress without ending the stage; continue the actual work. Difficulty or artifact incompletion alone is not a mathematical gap.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"obstacle_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["obstacle_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of check_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of submit_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"probe_library","description":"Query a proved Mathlib theorem and its exact signature/axioms in the offline sandbox. Returns located evidence for an M source; the mathematical statement and applicability still require review.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"declaration":{"type":"string"},"module":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","declaration","module"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_draft","description":"Read a JSON pointer in your own same-stage candidate after an actual structural check. No other file/stage is accessible; choose a narrow pointer for large objects.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"}},"required":["candidate","pointer"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false}],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":false,"prompt_cache_key":"b0127df8-1989-4c37-aa43-dca1c58fb5fe","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"low"},"top_p":0.98,"top_logprobs":0,"temperature":1.0,"reasoning":{"effort":"high","context":"all_turns","summary":null,"mode":"standard"},"user":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":38481,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":13568,"cache_write_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1604,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":308},"total_tokens":40085,"attribution":{"items":{"fc_0a1990edceb2c9e4016adb69ebd58481919711a8ee7960807a":{"input_tokens":31,"cached_tokens":31,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_0a1990edceb2c9e4016adb69eed14